schemaVersion: 1
id: goosetest-first-release
title: "goosetest: First-Release Implementation Plan"
heroTitle:
  lead: First
  accent: release.
firstStorySummary: Establish the compiler baseline and style rules before shaping the public API.
project: goosetest
status: planned
generatedAt: "2026-10-26T22:54:02+01:00"
scope: "A Goose-native assertion runtime and automatic test runner with strict unit mirrors, separate integration suites, explicit lifecycle semantics, and style-guide compliance."
summary[3]: Build goosetest from the reference POCs in ./poc using discovered test_* functions as the primary authoring model. Unit tests mirror src/ into test/; integration/ contains cross-module tests without a mirror requirement. This layout was explicitly selected by the user.,"Deliver working slices: an importable runtime, read-only project discovery, one-command compilation/execution, fixture and selection semantics, readable diagnostics, and self-hosted verification with a representative goosefmt consumer. Reuse the POC ideas while replacing silent truncation, brittle line scanning, and discarded exit codes.","Use /Users/bob/repos/goosefmt/docs/styleguide.md as the normative code/design guide. Keep the runtime standard-library-only and isolate the minimal native CLI adapter required by the installed compiler. The scope is a maintainable first release, not the POC’s full list of aspirational features. Concrete API, file-layout, lifecycle, command, and console references appear in the epic descriptions, starting at E1; every story links to the relevant original POC/style-guide sources."
