      - id: E2.S2
        title: Tokenize supported test declarations and preserve locations
        details[7]: "Build a focused lexical scanner for identifiers, strings and escapes, raw strings, character literals, nested block comments, line comments, and delimiters. Reuse design lessons from goosefmt without coupling to its whole formatter or importing its repository by absolute path.","Recognize one declared namespace per test file, top-level test_* functions, an optional Fixture struct, and named lifecycle hooks. Track brace depth so declarations inside strings, comments, or nested functions are not tests.","Record file, declaration line, namespace, function name, fixture participation, and hook signatures in a manifest. Use file path plus namespace plus function name as the stable case identity.","Support multiline signatures and optional inline on ordinary non-generic test functions. Reject unsupported generic, recursive, thread, foreign, or explicitly qualified test declarations with a source diagnostic.","Accept test functions with goosetest::Test& and an optional local Fixture&. Validate the supported hook forms without pretending to replace compiler type checking.",Parse immediately attached @DisplayName and @Disabled comments into optional manifest fields for E4. Reject malformed or unknown framework annotations; ordinary comments remain legal. Defer @Tag and @RepeatedTest explicitly.,"Use the concrete stable-ID spelling <relative test path>::<namespace>::<function> shown in the discovery reference; display names never affect identity."
        acceptanceCriteria[5]: A test declaration appears exactly once even when its signature spans lines or follows ordinary documentation.,Fake fn test_* text in strings and comments never enters the manifest.,Malformed declarations and metadata report a path and line instead of silently disappearing.,Duplicate case identities and suite namespaces that would collide at compile time are rejected before generation.,Scanning advances monotonically and stops at the configured nesting and byte limits.
        unitTests[2]: "Test escaped quotes, multiline raw strings, nested block comments, nested functions, and multiline parameters.",Check valid and invalid signatures and precise declaration line numbers with LF and CRLF input.
