      - id: E2.S3
        title: Enforce unit-test mirrors while admitting integration suites
        details[6]: "Require src/<path>/<name>.goose to correspond to test/<path>/<name>_test.goose and audit in both directions. Missing and orphaned unit files are errors, not informational warnings.",Discover integration/**/*_test.goose independently; integration tests may import multiple production modules and require no source counterpart.,"Require each discovered test file to have at least one valid test declaration. Allow shared test helpers only outside the audited test roots, in test_support/, so helper files do not masquerade as mirrors.","Keep root entry files, package facades, native code, and generated output outside the src/test mirror contract. Do not add exclusion globs or per-file exemptions in this release.",Audit the complete tree before applying any execution filter. Use sorted-path merge or a bounded lookup table for matching rather than the POC quadratic comparison.,"Report correspondence counts as mirror audit results, never as statement, branch, or behavioral coverage."
        acceptanceCriteria[4]: A valid mirrored project plus a cross-module integration suite passes the audit.,"A missing source counterpart, missing unit counterpart, bad test filename, or empty test file fails with its expected relative path.",Selecting one test does not hide a mirror violation elsewhere in the project.,Renaming a source module produces both the useful missing-mirror and orphan-test diagnostics.
        unitTests[2]: "Test exact matches, missing and orphaned pairs, similarly prefixed filenames, and integration-only additions.",Run the original POC sample and verify that src/workspaces/archive.goose is reported as missing a unit mirror.
