        title: Expose list and check-mirror through a small CLI
        details[5]: "Add root main.goose as CLI wiring and focused argument parsing/dispatch modules. Define goosetest list, goosetest check-mirror, and --project PATH; default the project to the current directory.","List stable case IDs, test source locations, unit/integration kind, and any recognized disabled reason. Emit deterministic plain text without terminal-specific dependencies.","Return 0 on a valid audit/list, 2 on invalid arguments, invalid project structure, read errors, or discovery errors. Reserve 1 for executed test failures.",Both commands use the same manifest and mirror implementation that the execution command will consume. Neither invokes the compiler or writes generated source.,Add clear help text including the conventions and limits. Avoid adding a custom TOML/YAML settings parser for the first release.
