    shortTitle: Project discovery
  - id: E3
    title: Compile and execute an entire project with one command
    summary: "Deliver goosetest test with generated static calls, ordinary Goose package resolution, bounded compiler/runner subprocesses, and truthful exit status."
    description: "<a id=\"reference-test-root\"></a>\n\n### Target one-time test root: my_app/goosetest_root.goose\n\n```goose\n// Declares test dependencies and invokes generated orchestration.\nimport goosetest from \"../goosetest\";\n\nimport goosetest_generated.runner;\n\nfn main() -> i32 {\n    return goosetest_generated::run_all();\n}\n```\n\nThis example assumes `my_app/` and the framework checkout are siblings as shown in the layout. A consumer using a published package replaces the source with its actual pinned repository reference. No repository URL is invented here. Extra application packages are declared in this root using ordinary Goose imports. An optional `goosetest_root.build` remains beside it for the compiler’s normal sidecar handling.\n\nThe root is authored once. Adding a test changes only a test file; generation refreshes the imported orchestration. Preserve the root’s exit value: returning `i32` here fixes the POC bug where a summary code is assigned and discarded.\n\nCompiler contract: [Pinned compiler package/import contract — line 92, `**Only the root file declares packages.**`](/Users/bob/.local/share/goose/v2026.3/goose-v2026.3-macos-arm64/docs/packages.md). Existing generator: [POC mirror audit and generation — line 266, `fn generate_junit_runner`](/Users/bob/repos/goosetest/poc/junit_runner_poc.goose). Existing summary status: [POC console summary — line 235, `fn summary`](/Users/bob/repos/goosetest/poc/example_project/goosetest.goose).\n\n<a id=\"reference-run-pipeline\"></a>\n\n### Target run flow and generated responsibility\n\n```text\ngoosetest test --project ./my_app\n  -> discover src/, test/, integration/\n  -> validate declarations and complete unit mirrors\n  -> select executable case IDs\n  -> write owned goosetest_generated/ modules\n  -> goose build --debug goosetest_root.goose\n  -> execute the newly built binary in the project directory\n  -> return 0 (pass), 1 (test/hook failure), or 2 (runner error)\n```\n\nGenerated code must contain statically visible calls to each discovered function under a `goosetest::run_case` boundary, including unreachable wrappers for disabled/filtered cases. It may split wrappers across multiple modules to satisfy the style limits. The exact generated helper names are implementation details; original source IDs, call-graph validity, and behavior are the contract.\n\nConcrete commands to support by the end of the plan:\n\n```sh\ngoosetest check-mirror --project ./my_app\ngoosetest list --project ./my_app\ngoosetest test --project ./my_app\ngoosetest test --project ./my_app --suite integration\ngoosetest test --project ./my_app --filter test_viewer_cannot_write --fail-fast\n```\n\nThe pipeline and commands are target behavior, not commands available in the current POC. The native subprocess adapter is new work: the existing scanner generates code but does not implement a safe process-launch stage.\n\nDelivery: fixture-free projects can run end to end. The stable test root is intentional one-time package wiring, not manual test registration. The small CLI native adapter is required by the pinned standard library, not an external dependency framework."
    dependencies[2]: E1,E2
    stories[4]:
      - id: E3.S1
        title: Generate suite code behind a stable Goose test root
        details[6]: "Use a checked-in goosetest_root.goose at the consumer project root. It declares import goosetest from the chosen local directory or pinned repository, declares other packages, imports goosetest_generated.runner, and returns goosetest_generated::run_all() from main.",Keep the test root stable so its relative package imports and optional goosetest_root.build sidecar retain normal compiler semantics. Do not copy dependency declarations out of production main files or infer a package manager.,"Generate suite modules under goosetest_generated/ from the manifest. Use direct compile-time calls enclosed by the runtime boundary, not runtime function registries or escaping closures.",All generated files directly import the modules they reference. Escape path and display strings as Goose literals using a dedicated encoder; validate identifiers separately.,Generate one bounded case wrapper per test and hierarchical dispatch helpers. Split suite and dispatch modules so generated files and functions obey the same 500-line and 70-line limits at scale.,Preserve source metadata in generated calls so runtime diagnostics name original test files rather than only generator output. Start with fixture-free test signatures; E4 adds lifecycle behavior.
        acceptanceCriteria[5]: The real example compiles through goosetest_root.goose and runs every discovered fixture-free case once in deterministic order.,Adding a valid test file requires no registration-list edit.,Local package imports remain correct when launched from another working directory and when the project root contains spaces.,A fixture with a native package or test-root sidecar compiles without rewriting its path semantics.,Generated code passes goosefmt check without running a formatter as part of normal test execution.
        unitTests[2]: "Compile generated fixtures with local package imports, escaped labels, and many discovered cases.",Check deterministic emitted source and original-source attribution on a failing case.
        filesLikelyTouched[8]: src/generation/runner.goose,src/generation/suites.goose,src/generation/literals.goose,goosetest_root.goose,examples/basic/goosetest_root.goose,test/generation/runner_test.goose,test/generation/suites_test.goose,test/generation/literals_test.goose
        dependencies[2]: E1.S4,E2.S4
        risk: high
        description: "**Design target:** [Concrete example in this plan](#reference-test-root).\n\n**Existing source references:**\n\n- [POC discovery and lifecycle emission — line 126, `fn scan_and_emit_suite`](/Users/bob/repos/goosetest/poc/junit_runner_poc.goose)\n- [POC mirror audit and generation — line 266, `fn generate_junit_runner`](/Users/bob/repos/goosetest/poc/junit_runner_poc.goose)\n- [Pinned compiler package/import contract — line 92, `**Only the root file declares packages.**`](/Users/bob/.local/share/goose/v2026.3/goose-v2026.3-macos-arm64/docs/packages.md)\n\n**Retain or change:** Generate static calls behind the authored test root; preserve compiler-native dependency resolution."
      - id: E3.S2
        title: Implement the minimal native process boundary
        details[6]: "The installed os.goose provides filesystem and environment operations but no subprocess API. Add one canonical Goose FFI module and a CLI-only native implementation, compiled through main.build; keep the importable runtime pure Goose.","Launch argv arrays directly using the supported platform process API. Set the child working directory explicitly; never construct a shell command from project paths, compiler paths, or test metadata.","Return a named ProcessResult distinguishing normal exit, launch failure, signal termination, cancellation, and deadline expiry. Preserve useful native error details without exposing an opaque wait status as a test result.","Inherit standard streams initially. Avoid pipe capture, output buffering, and protocol parsers until required; this prevents a stalled pipe from hanging a test run.",Use finite stage deadlines and a bounded termination grace period. Use a monotonic clock and the platform process-group facilities to terminate and reap the stage on timeout or interruption.,"Keep extern declarations unique, with const slice/reference inputs where required. Support the available macOS arm64 platform first; document the boundary for future ports without claiming untested platform support."
        acceptanceCriteria[5]: "Arguments containing spaces, quotes, dollar signs, and semicolons arrive literally in the child.",Missing executables and nonzero child exits are distinguishable.,A hung fixture terminates within its deadline plus the documented grace period and leaves no owned child process running.,Cancellation and signal termination never become a passing test result.,An application importing the runtime alone does not link the process adapter.
        unitTests[2]: "Use purpose-built child fixtures for argv echo, selected exit codes, deliberate signal termination, and waiting indefinitely.","Exercise deadline expiry and interruption, checking child reaping from outside the adapter."
        filesLikelyTouched[5]: main.build,src/platform/process.goose,native/process.c,integration/process_test.goose,test/platform/process_test.goose
        dependencies[1]: E1.S1
        risk: high
        description: "**Design target:** [Concrete example in this plan](#reference-run-pipeline).\n\n**Existing source references:**\n\n- [Pinned standard-library OS surface](/Users/bob/.local/share/goose/v2026.3/goose-v2026.3-macos-arm64/stdlib/os.goose)\n- [Style guide: canonical foreign declarations — line 140, `### 2.6`](/Users/bob/repos/goosefmt/docs/styleguide.md)\n- [Pinned compiler package/import contract — line 92, `**Only the root file declares packages.**`](/Users/bob/.local/share/goose/v2026.3/goose-v2026.3-macos-arm64/docs/packages.md)\n\n**Retain or change:** This is new CLI work: the prototype does not supply a subprocess adapter, and the pinned OS module has no launch API."
      - id: E3.S3
        title: "Wire discovery, compilation, execution, and exit policy"
        details[6]: "Implement goosetest test: validate CLI options, discover and audit, generate source, compile the stable test root, and run the resulting binary only after a successful build.",Use goose build --debug as the first-release execution path so native packages and runtime checks behave consistently. Expose --compiler PATH plus --compile-timeout-seconds and --run-timeout-seconds as ordinary execution options with finite documented defaults.,Set both child stages to the project working directory. Execute the newly built output using an exact path and prevent reuse of an old binary after a compilation failure.,"Define status 0 as a completed run with no failed cases, 1 as one or more ordinary test/hook failures, and 2 as discovery, compilation, artifact, process, timeout, or incomplete-run errors. Preserve conventional cancellation status if the parent is interrupted.",A run that discovers or selects zero cases is an error. A nonempty selection consisting entirely of explicitly disabled cases is a valid skipped run once E4 lands.,"Do not promise continuation after fatal Goose checks, exit calls, foreign crashes, or a hung test. These fail the run; per-case process isolation and contained-worker assertions remain outside this release."
        acceptanceCriteria[5]: "One command returns the correct shell status for passing, assertion-failing, uncompilable, and runtime-crashing projects.",The next ordinary case executes after a framework assertion failure.,"The runner never starts when the audit, generation, or compiler stage fails.",No tests and no matching tests cannot produce a misleading green result.,Timeout messages identify whether compilation or execution exceeded its deadline.
        unitTests[2]: "Run process-level fixtures for every status category, including a stale executable left beside a newly broken source tree.",Verify working-directory behavior with a test reading a project-relative resource.
        filesLikelyTouched[7]: src/cli.goose,src/arguments.goose,src/execution/command.goose,integration/execution_test.goose,test/cli_test.goose,test/arguments_test.goose,test/execution/command_test.goose
        dependencies[2]: E3.S1,E3.S2
        risk: high
        description: "**Design target:** [Concrete example in this plan](#reference-run-pipeline).\n\n**Existing source references:**\n\n- [POC console summary — line 235, `fn summary`](/Users/bob/repos/goosetest/poc/example_project/goosetest.goose)\n- [POC mirror audit and generation — line 266, `fn generate_junit_runner`](/Users/bob/repos/goosetest/poc/junit_runner_poc.goose)\n- [Style guide: error propagation — line 674, `### 6.6`](/Users/bob/repos/goosefmt/docs/styleguide.md)\n\n**Retain or change:** Return the real status shown in the output reference instead of assigning and discarding it."
      - id: E3.S4
        title: Own generated artifacts without stale or destructive behavior
        details[6]: Reserve goosetest_generated/ for framework artifacts with an ownership marker. Refuse to overwrite a preexisting unowned directory or a user-authored test root.,"Write generated source atomically, compare content to avoid needless rewrites, and keep deterministic filenames independent of timestamps.","Update the generated root only after all referenced suite files are ready. On interrupted generation, the next run must regenerate successfully before compiling; no cached result is trusted.",Remove obsolete generated files only when they are in the owned directory and listed by the previous generation manifest. Never recursively delete user paths.,Fail clearly on concurrent invocations targeting the same output directory using a narrow exclusive-ownership mechanism. Do not add a scheduler or parallel execution.,Add generated artifacts to repository ignore rules. Keep generated source after a failure for inspection; keep documentation clear that it is disposable.
        acceptanceCriteria[4]: Deleting or renaming a test does not leave a stale generated call on the next run.,A second run with unchanged input produces the same source bytes and avoids rewriting unchanged source files.,"An unowned directory, read-only output location, or concurrent run produces status 2 with no user-file deletion.",A failed write cannot lead to execution of a stale successful binary.
        unitTests[2]: "Simulate obsolete generated files, an interrupted generation, and a write failure in temporary project roots.",Attempt a concurrent invocation and verify that exactly one process owns generation.
