    shortTitle: Compile & execute
  - id: E4
    title: "Fixtures, lifecycle hooks, disabled tests, and focused runs"
    summary: "Deliver the POC authoring experience with precise failure semantics, including setup failures and disabled/filtered functions that remain valid in Goose’s call graph."
    description: "<a id=\"reference-lifecycle\"></a>\n\n### Target fixture and lifecycle behavior\n\nUse the [complete auth test file](#reference-unit-api) as the ordinary fixture example. For a hook that needs framework assertions, the supported alternative is:\n\n```goose\nfn before_each(t: goosetest::Test&, f: Fixture&) {\n    f.header = \"Bearer tok_admin\";\n    t.assert_true(f.header.len > 0, \"fixture must provide a header\");\n}\n```\n\nThis replaces the fixture-only `before_each` in that file; do not define both forms. The fresh fixture must be safe to clean up even if setup stops partway through initialization.\n\n| Trigger | Required behavior |\n| --- | --- |\n| Normal fixture-using case | Default fixture → before_each → test body → after_each → final case result. |\n| Framework assertion fails in setup | Record setup failure → omit body → attempt after_each once → one failed case. |\n| Body and cleanup both fail | Keep both phase diagnostics → one failed case. |\n| Fixture-free case in the same file | Execute with Test only; do not construct Fixture or call fixture-specific hooks. |\n| before_all fails | Record suite error → skip its executable cases → attempt after_all → continue other suites. |\n| Disabled or filtered case | Typecheck its wrapper; do not execute its body, fixture construction, or per-case hooks. |\n| --fail-fast after ordinary failure | Finish current cleanup and suite cleanup, then stop additional bodies. |\n| Fatal runtime abort or timeout | Report an incomplete run; no cleanup promise. |\n\nExisting prototype orchestration: [POC discovery and lifecycle emission — line 126, `fn scan_and_emit_suite`](/Users/bob/repos/goosetest/poc/junit_runner_poc.goose). Disabled-call-graph technique: [Disabled call-graph preservation — line 224, `Keep disabled test in`](/Users/bob/repos/goosetest/poc/junit_runner_poc.goose). The separate contained-worker prototype is deferred: [Deferred contained-worker alternative — line 46, `fn expect_abort`](/Users/bob/repos/goosetest/poc/goosetest_contained_poc.goose).\n\n<a id=\"reference-integration-api\"></a>\n\n### Target integration file: integration/access_flow_test.goose\n\n```goose\n// Verifies that token parsing and permission decisions agree across modules.\nnamespace access_flow_test;\n\nimport goosetest;\n\nimport src.auth.token;\nimport src.workspaces.permissions;\n\nfn test_viewer_token_cannot_write(t: goosetest::Test&) {\n    let header = \"Bearer tok_viewer\";\n    let claims = auth_token::parse_bearer(header);\n    let decision = workspaces_permissions::check_write_access(header);\n    t.assert_true(claims.valid);\n    t.assert_eq(claims.scope, decision.effective_role);\n    t.assert_false(decision.allowed);\n}\n```\n\nIntegration tests use the same Test API, assertions, metadata, and failure rules. Their distinction is discovery and layout: this case intentionally tests agreement between two modules and has no matching `src/access_flow.goose` requirement.\n\nDelivery: the main POC fixtures and disabled-test workflow are usable, with narrower and honest cleanup guarantees. Repetition, tags, nested describe blocks, parameterized cases, and arbitrary hook graphs are intentionally deferred."
    dependencies[1]: E3.S3
    stories[4]:
      - id: E4.S1
        title: "Run fresh fixtures with separate setup, test, and cleanup boundaries"
        details[7]: Instantiate one default-initialized Fixture per selected case when its signature requests it. A file may mix fixture-free and fixture-using test functions; do not infer a function signature solely from the presence of a Fixture declaration.,"Support before_each(f: Fixture&) and after_each(f: Fixture&) from the POC, plus forms accepting goosetest::Test& first when a hook needs framework assertions. Reject ambiguous duplicate hook forms.","Execute setup, body, and cleanup through separate recoverable boundaries, each labeled with its phase. Cleanup receives the same fixture even after a framework setup or body failure.","If setup records any failure, skip the body but attempt cleanup once. Require the default fixture to be safe to clean up after partial initialization and document this contract.",A cleanup failure is appended alongside an existing failure; it never replaces the original cause. Report one failed case with multiple phase diagnostics.,Do not use a defer feature absent from the pinned compiler or claim cleanup after process termination or a fatal runtime abort.,"For mixed signatures, fixture construction and fixture-specific before_each/after_each hooks apply only to tests requesting Fixture&; a Test-only function runs without them, as shown in the lifecycle reference."
        acceptanceCriteria[5]: Fixtures start with default state for every case and cannot leak mutations to the next case.,Setup failure prevents body execution but still reaches cleanup exactly once.,Body failure plus cleanup failure retains both diagnostics and counts one failed case.,A fixture-free function in the same file receives only its declared argument and compiles.,A fixture-free test beside fixture-using tests causes no fixture-construction or fixture-hook side effects.
        unitTests[2]: "Record phase sentinels for pass, setup failure, body failure, cleanup failure, and combined failure.",Test a default/partially initialized fixture cleanup and a mixed-signature suite.
        filesLikelyTouched[7]: src/generation/suites.goose,src/runtime/execution.goose,src/runtime/results.goose,integration/lifecycle_test.goose,test/runtime/execution_test.goose,test/runtime/results_test.goose,test/generation/suites_test.goose
        dependencies[1]: E3.S3
        risk: high
        description: "**Design target:** [Concrete example in this plan](#reference-lifecycle).\n\n**Existing source references:**\n\n- [Auth test authoring example — line 12, `struct Fixture`](/Users/bob/repos/goosetest/poc/example_project/test/auth/token_test.goose)\n- [POC discovery and lifecycle emission — line 126, `fn scan_and_emit_suite`](/Users/bob/repos/goosetest/poc/junit_runner_poc.goose)\n- [Runtime recovery boundary — line 56, `fn run_case`](/Users/bob/repos/goosetest/poc/example_project/goosetest.goose)\n\n**Retain or change:** Keep familiar hook names but use separate recovery boundaries and retain the original failure if cleanup also fails."
      - id: E4.S2
        title: Define suite-level setup and cleanup outcomes
        details[5]: "Support before_all()/after_all() and optional goosetest::Test& forms for recoverable hook assertions. Do not introduce shared fixture objects or dependency injection.",Run suite hooks only for a suite with at least one selected executable case. An entirely disabled or entirely filtered suite has no lifecycle side effects.,"A failed before_all prevents that suite’s test bodies, records a suite-level failure, and marks otherwise executable selected cases as skipped because setup failed. Attempt after_all exactly once.",A failed after_all makes the run fail even if every case passed. Keep suite-hook failures separate from case totals and report their phase clearly.,"Define state lifetime and reset points so a previous suite failure cannot contaminate the next suite, and a successful later suite cannot erase the earlier error."
        acceptanceCriteria[4]: Suite setup and cleanup run once around multiple selected cases in the expected order.,Before-all failure skips only that suite’s executable cases; another suite still executes.,After-all failure returns status 1 and is visible without fabricating an ordinary test case.,A suite with no executable selected cases runs neither suite hook.
        unitTests[2]: Check phase order across two suites and the outcome of failing setup or cleanup.,Test empty executable selections and all-disabled suites after E4.S3 is integrated.
        filesLikelyTouched[7]: src/generation/suites.goose,src/runtime/execution.goose,src/runtime/results.goose,integration/lifecycle_test.goose,test/runtime/execution_test.goose,test/runtime/results_test.goose,test/generation/suites_test.goose
