        description: "**Design target:** [Concrete example in this plan](#reference-lifecycle).\n\n**Existing source references:**\n\n- [POC discovery and lifecycle emission — line 126, `fn scan_and_emit_suite`](/Users/bob/repos/goosetest/poc/junit_runner_poc.goose)\n- [Style guide: error propagation — line 674, `### 6.6`](/Users/bob/repos/goosefmt/docs/styleguide.md)\n\n**Retain or change:** Make the table’s suite-hook and no-executable-case behavior observable."
      - id: E4.S3
        title: Preserve disabled cases and display names safely
        details[5]: "Implement the already scanned // @DisplayName(\"...\") and // @Disabled(\"reason\") metadata. Require a nonempty disabled reason and correctly decode supported string escapes.","Generate an unreachable, typechecked execution wrapper for every disabled test. Keep the run_case ancestor required by long-distance assertions even when the test will never execute.","Keep fixture construction and relevant hook references well typed within the unreachable path, without evaluating any of them at runtime.","Report disabled cases as skipped with their stable identity, optional display label, and reason. Display labels do not replace identity or make duplicate labels illegal.","Reject @Tag, @RepeatedTest, and other unsupported framework annotations with a direct explanation rather than accepting comments that have no effect."
        acceptanceCriteria[4]: A disabled test with a framework assertion compiles and never changes a runtime sentinel.,"A type error inside a disabled test fails compilation, preserving the POC’s no-bit-rot behavior.","Quoted labels and reasons survive parsing, generation, and output without source injection or corruption.",A valid all-disabled selection exits 0 and reports the actual skip count.
        unitTests[2]: "Compile disabled pass/fail assertions, deliberately type-invalid disabled bodies, and fixture signatures.",Verify that disabled suite-only selection runs neither construction side effects nor hooks.
