        dependencies[3]: E3.S4,E4.S4,E5.S3
        risk: high
        description: "**Design target:** [Concrete example in this plan](#reference-project-layout).\n\n**Existing source references:**\n\n- [POC mirror audit and generation — line 266, `fn generate_junit_runner`](/Users/bob/repos/goosetest/poc/junit_runner_poc.goose)\n- [Auth test authoring example — line 12, `struct Fixture`](/Users/bob/repos/goosetest/poc/example_project/test/auth/token_test.goose)\n- [Style guide: file/declaration structure — line 58, `### 2.1`](/Users/bob/repos/goosefmt/docs/styleguide.md)\n\n**Retain or change:** Use the same mirrored layout and authoring experience for the framework itself."
      - id: E6.S2
        title: Lock down the regressions that could create false success
        details[5]: "Build a focused external regression matrix for failed assertions, compile errors, runtime aborts, empty selection, malformed metadata, missing mirrors, discovery limits, failed output writes, stale binaries, and stage timeouts.","Include large-but-bounded discovery and generation fixtures that cross the POC’s 64-case/128-file thresholds. Verify completeness by exact case IDs and counts, not elapsed-time measurements.","Exercise disabled and filtered tests that contain non-local assertion returns, plus setup/body/cleanup combinations.",Keep process and filesystem fixtures isolated under owned temporary directories and always clean up resources they created. Do not rely on success of the system under test to validate the oracle.,Run the supported debug build path. Add release-mode compiler checks only where a concrete semantic concern requires them; do not create a compiler/platform matrix without a support commitment.
        acceptanceCriteria[4]: Every incomplete or failed-run fixture produces its specified nonzero status and an actionable diagnostic.,No test disappears silently when a POC-era capacity is exceeded within the new limits.,Disabled/filtered type errors are detected and no stale executable runs after a failed compile.,Timeout/cancellation fixtures leave no framework-owned processes or locks behind.
        unitTests[2]: Execute the process-level regression matrix through the independent verifier.,Check exact discovered/generated case identities on bounded large fixtures.
        filesLikelyTouched[4]: scripts/verify.goose,integration/failure_contract_test.goose,integration/limits_test.goose,integration/fixtures/README.md
        dependencies[1]: E6.S1
        risk: high
        description: "**Design target:** [Concrete example in this plan](#reference-console).\n\n**Existing source references:**\n\n- [POC directory walker — line 33, `fn walk_goose_files`](/Users/bob/repos/goosetest/poc/junit_runner_poc.goose)\n- [Disabled call-graph preservation — line 224, `Keep disabled test in`](/Users/bob/repos/goosetest/poc/junit_runner_poc.goose)\n- [POC console summary — line 235, `fn summary`](/Users/bob/repos/goosetest/poc/example_project/goosetest.goose)\n- [Deferred contained-worker alternative — line 46, `fn expect_abort`](/Users/bob/repos/goosetest/poc/goosetest_contained_poc.goose)\n\n**Retain or change:** Turn prototype failure modes into external exit/completeness assertions; contained workers are reference evidence only."
      - id: E6.S3
        title: Demonstrate adoption with goosefmt without changing that repository
        details[5]: Create a disposable consumer fixture based on representative pure formatter/lexer behavior in /Users/bob/repos/goosefmt. Preserve its production implementation and expected behavior while converting the selected tests to goosetest conventions.,"Include a lexer unit mirror, a formatter unit mirror, and one integration test spanning tokenization and formatting. Include realistic strings, nested comments, and custom diagnostic messages.",Resolve source and package paths explicitly in the fixture; do not make the distributed framework depend on /Users/bob/repos/goosefmt.,"Identify adoption changes needed for the real repository, whose current tests live in src/tests.goose and whose CLI entry is under src/. Document the mapping to src/test mirrors and an appropriate root entry.","Do not edit goosefmt, migrate its entire test suite, or publish a change to that repository as part of this plan. The artifact is a reproducible consumer example and a concrete migration recipe."
        acceptanceCriteria[4]: Representative existing behavior passes through the public package and generated runner in the disposable consumer.,An intentionally changed formatter expectation produces a useful value/field diagnostic and status 1.,The fixture demonstrates unit mirrors and a separate integration suite together.,The original goosefmt working tree and test commands remain untouched.
        unitTests[2]: Run representative known formatter/lexer cases before and after their conversion in the isolated fixture.,Verify a deliberate negative expectation and package resolution outside the goosetest source tree.
        filesLikelyTouched[3]: integration/consumer_test.goose,integration/fixtures/goosefmt/README.md,docs/adopting_goosefmt.md
        dependencies[1]: E6.S2
        risk: medium
        description: "**Design target:** [Concrete example in this plan](#reference-integration-api).\n\n**Existing source references:**\n\n- [Existing goosefmt behavioral tests — line 89, `fn test_statement_blocks`](/Users/bob/repos/goosefmt/src/tests.goose)\n- [Existing goosefmt tokenizer — line 15, `struct Token`](/Users/bob/repos/goosefmt/src/lexer.goose)\n- [Normative Goose style guide](/Users/bob/repos/goosefmt/docs/styleguide.md)\n\n**Retain or change:** Validate real consumer behavior in the separate integration area without migrating the original repository."
      - id: E6.S4
        title: "Finish developer commands, examples, and first-release documentation"
        details[6]: "Provide Taskfile targets for building, testing, and checking style, with repository automation implemented in scripts/*.goose and long-form CLI options. Keep tasks thin; do not add a release service or deployment system.","Document package installation by explicit local source or pinned repository reference, one-time goosetest_root.goose wiring, the optional test-root native sidecar, directory layout, assertions, fixtures, selection, status codes, and finite default limits/deadlines.","Document unsupported features: tags, repetitions, parameterized cases, nested describe DSL, contained-worker APIs, per-case crash isolation, parallel runs, property testing, snapshots, watch mode, exporters, and unverified operating systems.",Apply the style guide to all shipping examples and generated code. Retain poc/ as historical reference with an explicit exclusion from shipping-source checks; explain its known violations instead of presenting it as conforming framework code.,Update POC documentation references from obsolete docs/ locations where needed and label historical performance/cleanup claims as prototype claims. Do not rewrite the POC into a second supported implementation.,"Run the required checks once the final changes are complete, then record the supported baseline and reproducible commands."
        acceptanceCriteria[6]: "A clean checkout with documented prerequisites can build the CLI, run the passing example, run self-tests, and check style using the documented commands.",The first example has no intentional failures by default and needs no manual list of tests.,Every shipped .goose file and representative generated project passes goosefmt check; intentional invalid fixture data and historical POCs are clearly scoped out.,"Documentation distinguishes ordinary assertion failures, runner errors, disabled cases, and fatal runtime failures.","No benchmarks, telemetry/metrics, feature-flag system, shadow/A-B rollout, or smoke-check workflow is introduced.","The embedded unit, integration, and test-root examples are compiled and style checked as maintained documentation examples; source references and public signatures match the implementation."
        unitTests[2]: Execute the documented build/test/check commands and the basic consumer walkthrough.,Read the generated public API and CLI documentation against implemented behavior; do not add tests that merely restate documentation.
        filesLikelyTouched[6]: README.md,Taskfile.yml,scripts/check.goose,docs/architecture.md,docs/compatibility.md,poc/goosetest_framework_research.md
        dependencies[1]: E6.S3
        risk: medium
        description: "**Design target:** [Concrete example in this plan](#framework-design-reference).\n\n**Existing source references:**\n\n- [Normative Goose style guide](/Users/bob/repos/goosefmt/docs/styleguide.md)\n- [Style guide: Goose repository tooling — line 155, `### 2.7`](/Users/bob/repos/goosefmt/docs/styleguide.md)\n- [POC design research — line 61, `## Part 2:`](/Users/bob/repos/goosetest/poc/goosetest_framework_research.md)\n\n**Retain or change:** Promote the embedded reference examples to maintained user documentation, and keep their commands and results truthful."
    shortTitle: Release & adoption
recommendedOrder[23]{ref,reason}:
  E1.S1,First fix the compiler and style baseline; this avoids later public-API and generation rework.
  E1.S2,Prove the central hard/soft assertion semantics immediately.
  E1.S3,Stabilize bounded ownership and result records before adding consumers.
  E1.S4,Finish the first usable vertical slice and independently verify shell status.
  E2.S1,Start discovery as an independent track; it can begin after E1.S1 if work is delegated.
  E2.S2,Build declaration scanning independently of runtime and process code.
  E2.S3,Join paths and declarations into the agreed strict-unit/separate-integration contract.
  E2.S4,Ship useful list/audit commands before compilation integration.
  E3.S2,Prove the necessary native process/deadline boundary early; this can run in parallel with E2 after E1.S1.
  E3.S1,Connect the usable runtime and manifest using the stable root/package model.
  E3.S3,Deliver one-command test execution and real status propagation.
  E3.S4,Make repeated and interrupted runs safe before broad self-hosting.
  E5.S1,Improve diagnostics on the stable runtime; this track can start after E1.S4 without waiting for E3.
  E5.S2,Add the high-value POC field diffs without general deep-comparison machinery.
  E5.S3,"Finish a reporter against stable results, ready for lifecycle phases."
  E4.S1,Add per-case fixtures and separate failure boundaries after the basic runner works.
  E4.S2,Extend proven per-case semantics to suite hooks.
  E4.S3,Protect disabled tests against runtime side effects and compile-time bit rot.
  E4.S4,Add focused execution and fail-fast only after cleanup/disabled behavior is settled.
  E6.S1,Join the completed features by running the framework through its own runner.
  E6.S2,Use an independent oracle to catch false-success regressions.
  E6.S3,Validate real-consumer ergonomics in an isolated goosefmt fixture.
  E6.S4,Finalize instructions and run required release checks against the finished implementation.
exitCriteria[9]: A documented consumer project with mirrored units and independent integration tests builds and runs with one goosetest test invocation.,"Passing, assertion-failing, disabled, empty, compile-error, runtime-abort, timeout, and limit-breach outcomes have independently verified process statuses.",Discovery and generation are deterministic and complete within their bounds; no test or failure is silently dropped.,"Fixture and suite cleanup semantics are tested for setup/body/cleanup failure combinations, including preservation of original failures.",Disabled and filtered functions retain valid non-local-return ancestry and remain compiler checked.,The framework runs its own mirrored unit/integration suite and is checked by a small independent process-level oracle.,A disposable goosefmt consumer demonstrates real adoption without modifying the original repository.,"Shipping source, example source, and representative generated output pass the specified style checks; historical POCs and invalid fixture data are explicitly identified.",All required commands and platform/compiler limitations are documented; excluded features and operational fluff have not entered the implementation.
